   The beam finds sieve-complete high-coverage sets; some even defeat
   the folded antipodal witness test.  They still have positive exact
   gaps and empty endpoint cores.  So the obstruction is not failure to
   guess the right gate; it is the inability to make the dyadic debt
   leafless after the sieve is paid.

6. Synthesis / proof targets left standing
   Route A: Folded antipodal plus endpoint-leaf theorem.  The fold alone
   can miss boundary-only structure, but any folded-danger set found by
   the beams still peels to empty endpoint core.  Prove that folded
   danger forces a private dyadic endpoint leaf.
   Route B: Local-cover rigidity.  The 16-gate's endpoint cover forces
   the nine-residue pattern (1,3,5,7,8,9,11,13,15) up to dilation.
   Prove that any five-speed completion keeps a positive fixed-threshold
   gap or a private endpoint leaf.
   Route C: 2-torsion moat.  The full normalized half-turn cube has a
   128-cell moat.  Prove non-half-turn residues are no better by a
   compression/rounding argument, then lift through endpoint debt.
   These are three different shadows of the same thing: in the pure
   2-adic row, every attempt to close a boundary creates a lower-layer
   private obligation before a labelled protection cycle can close.
